{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"UIKitTracking"}],"externalID":"UIKitTracking","title":"UIKitTracking"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module to track events from UIKit views, view controllers and controls on iOS, iPadOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tvOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst; elsewhere it builds empty, and on macOS and watchOS its API isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there. SwiftUI views use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and AppKit views on macOS use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracker is a UIKit trait, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackerTrait"},{"type":"text","text":". Set it on a window scene’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitOverrides"},{"type":"text","text":" as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scene connects, and every view controller and view in the scene’s windows inherits it, the way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI views inherit their environment. Read it in any of them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitCollection.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view controller or view can set its own for everything below it, and each scene keeps its own, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two windows can track through two trackers. Until a tracker is set, the trait holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.noOp"},{"type":"text","text":", which drops every event."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks an event each time a control sends the given control events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":".primaryActionTriggered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default), through the tracker the control’s traits hold at that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","import UIKit","","@Event","struct ShareTapped {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","final class CartViewController: UIViewController {","    let share = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","    let checkOut = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        share.track(ShareTapped())  \/\/ through the tracker the button's traits hold when it is tapped","        checkOut.addTarget(self, action: #selector(checkOut(_:)), for: .primaryActionTriggered)","        view.addSubview(share)","        view.addSubview(checkOut)","    }","","    @objc func checkOut(_ sender: UIButton) {","        sender.traitCollection.tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))","    }","}","","\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:):","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" adds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAction"},{"type":"text","text":" beside the control’s other actions and targets, so they still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run, and returns it; pass it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAction(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop tracking. Where SwiftUI hosts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UIKit, or UIKit hosts SwiftUI, the trait and SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" are one value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers all three frameworks.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"API","type":"heading","text":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where the module is empty, so its symbols have no pages","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them for an iOS target.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackerTrait"},{"text":": the trait holding the tracker, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.noOp"},{"text":" until one is set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UITraitCollection.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":": reads the trait."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIMutableTraits.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":": sets the trait on a window scene’s, view controller’s or view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitOverrides"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)"},{"text":": tracks an event each time the control sends the given control events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/uikittracking"]}],"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/appkittracking":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"AppKitTracking","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link","title":"AppKitTracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/swiftuitracking":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","title":"SwiftUITracking","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftUITracking","type":"codeVoice"}]},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"UIKitTracking","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","type":"topic"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingfromviews":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","type":"text"}]}}}